del-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="352">Thanks for sharing that transcript snippet â€” it helps a lot. In that interview (the debate with Eliezer Yudkowsky), Miller explicitly frames <strong data-start="141" data-end="191">technological progress as feeding â€œarms racesâ€</strong>. His point is that advances in software and computation simultaneously strengthen both the <em data-start="283" data-end="294">offensive</em> and the <em data-start="303" data-end="314">defensive</em> sides of different existential risks:</p>
<ul data-start="354" data-end="859">
<li data-start="354" data-end="492">
<p data-start="356" data-end="492"><strong data-start="356" data-end="381">Biological arms race:</strong> synthetic biology + tools like AlphaFold make engineered pathogens more feasible, while defenses lag behind.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="493" data-end="702">
<p data-start="495" data-end="702"><strong data-start="495" data-end="523">Cybersecurity arms race:</strong> DARPA had already shown that autonomous malware could discover and exploit vulnerabilities, which means the infrastructure underpinning civilization is â€œmassively insecurable.â€</p>
</li>
<li data-start="703" data-end="859">
<p data-start="705" data-end="859"><strong data-start="705" data-end="734">General small-kill risks:</strong> even without AGI, humanity already crossed thresholds where determined attackers could destabilize or collapse civilization.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="861" data-end="910">The key line you picked up on is where he says:</p>
<blockquote data-start="911" data-end="1070">
<p data-start="913" data-end="1070"><em data-start="913" data-end="1068">â€œAs we advance our ability to build software which is capable, it will amplify both sides of each of these arms races, of every one of these arms races.â€</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="1072" data-end="1370">Thatâ€™s the context for his perception of Big Tech too: each new leap in capabilityâ€”cloud, AI, genetic design platforms, networked commerceâ€”doesnâ€™t simply â€œadvance progress.â€ It escalates an <em data-start="1262" data-end="1294">interlocking set of arms races</em> where offense and defense chase each other, and the outcome is uncertain.</p>
<p data-start="1372" data-end="1598">So while he doesnâ€™t name-drop â€œBig Techâ€ directly in that moment, the underlying critique matches: the major tech firms are engines that accelerate these races, often without building adequate defensive infrastructure first.</p>
<p data-start="1600" data-end="1784" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to pull out and summarize <strong data-start="1641" data-end="1705">all the distinct â€œarms racesâ€ Miller lists in that interview</strong> (biosecurity, cybersecurity, AI, etc.), so you have them as a clean reference?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.4