ional figure in AI alignment, and **Mark Miller**, a computer security and decentralized systems expert, as they explore their differing perspectives on the **risks and potential futures of advanced artificial intelligence (AI)**. Both agree on the **ultimate goal of a flourishing future for humanity** but diverge sharply on the **least risky strategies to achieve it**. Their conversation navigates key points such as the **nature of intelligence (prediction versus steering)**, the **role of social and emergent intelligence in human civilization**, and the **potential for AI to either cooperate within a human-designed framework or autonomously lead to human extinction**. A central disagreement revolves around whether **delaying AI development and establishing robust, secure computational systems** can genuinely safeguard humanity against powerful, potentially misaligned superintelligences, or if such efforts are ultimately futile against an inherently destructive force.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex justify-end"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none duration-300 group-hover/turn-messages:delay-300 pointer-events-none opacity-0 motion-safe:transition-opacity group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:opacity-100 group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:opacity-100 has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:opacity-100" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.6