ords dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="78">Hereâ€™s how their <strong data-start="17" data-end="53">backgrounds shape their outlooks</strong> on AI risk and strategy:</p>
<hr data-start="80" data-end="83">
<h2 data-start="85" data-end="109"><strong data-start="88" data-end="109">Eliezer Yudkowsky</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="110" data-end="823">
<li data-start="110" data-end="288">
<p data-start="112" data-end="288"><strong data-start="112" data-end="127">Background:</strong> Founder of the Machine Intelligence Research Institute (MIRI); central figure in the â€œrationalistâ€ community; early writer on Friendly AI and the singularity.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="289" data-end="436">
<p data-start="291" data-end="436"><strong data-start="291" data-end="300">Lens:</strong> Philosophical and theoretical. He treats AI as an <strong data-start="351" data-end="371">agent with goals</strong> that could optimize reality in ways catastrophic for humanity.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="437" data-end="823">
<p data-start="439" data-end="462"><strong data-start="439" data-end="460">Impact on stance:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="465" data-end="823">
<li data-start="465" data-end="575">
<p data-start="467" data-end="575">Because he starts from agent-theoretic models, he sees misalignment as nearly inevitable and catastrophic.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="578" data-end="686">
<p data-start="580" data-end="686">This makes him deeply skeptical of partial measures like â€œmore secure computingâ€ or â€œbetter governance.â€</p>
</li>
<li data-start="689" data-end="823">
<p data-start="691" data-end="823">He emphasizes <strong data-start="705" data-end="742">pausing or halting AI development</strong>, since any progress toward AGI raises the chance of an uncontrollable runaway.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="825" data-end="828">
<h2 data-start="830" data-end="851"><strong data-start="833" data-end="851">Mark S. Miller</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="852" data-end="1731">
<li data-start="852" data-end="1072">
<p data-start="854" data-end="1072"><strong data-start="854" data-end="869">Background:</strong> Computer scientist, inventor of the E programming language, pioneer of capability-based security, long-time advocate of secure distributed systems. Experience at PARC, HP Labs, Google, and now Agoric.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1073" data-end="1222">
<p data-start="1075" data-end="1222"><strong data-start="1075" data-end="1084">Lens:</strong> Practical systems-building. He views civilization as already dependent on fragile computational substrates that are insecure by design.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1223" data-end="1731">
<p data-start="1225" data-end="1248"><strong data-start="1225" data-end="1246">Impact on stance:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1251" data-end="1731">
<li data-start="1251" data-end="1365">
<p data-start="1253" data-end="1365">He frames risks as <strong data-start="1272" data-end="1286">arms races</strong> already underway in cybersecurity, biosecurity, and decentralized computing.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1368" data-end="1619">
<p data-start="1370" data-end="1619">Because his career has been spent on <em data-start="1407" data-end="1441">hardening systems against misuse</em>, he believes the right move is to <strong data-start="1476" data-end="1530">build robust, capability-secure infrastructure now</strong>â€”so that AI emerges into an environment where cooperation and containment are possible.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1622" data-end="1731">
<p data-start="1624" data-end="1731">Heâ€™s less fatalistic than Yudkowsky: he thinks defenses can gain the upper hand if we engineer carefully.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1733" data-end="1736">
<h2 data-start="1738" data-end="1766"><strong data-start="1741" data-end="1766">The Resulting Tension</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="1767" data-end="2169">
<li data-start="1767" data-end="1844">
<p data-start="1769" data-end="1844">Yudkowskyâ€™s outlook: <strong data-start="1790" data-end="1842">Theoretical inevitability â†’ Doom unless we stop.</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1845" data-end="1924">
<p data-start="1847" data-end="1924">Millerâ€™s outlook: <strong data-start="1865" data-end="1922">Engineering pragmatism â†’ Resilience through security.</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1925" data-end="2169">
<p data-start="1927" data-end="2169">Both worry about existential collapse, but Yudkowsky sees <strong data-start="1985" data-end="2013">superintelligence itself</strong> as the unique trigger, while Miller sees <strong data-start="2055" data-end="2089">AI as one amplifier among many</strong> in a landscape already riddled with civilization-threatening vulnerabilities.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2171" data-end="2174">
