mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="73">Yes â€” thatâ€™s a really sharp analogy for <strong data-start="40" data-end="70">intersubjectivity collapse</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="75" data-end="288">When you think of Christianity, Islam, and atheism, youâ€™re looking at <strong data-start="145" data-end="245">value systems and interpretive languages that are not just different, but mutually contradictory</strong> at some points. Each comes with its own:</p>
<ul data-start="290" data-end="515">
<li data-start="290" data-end="366">
<p data-start="292" data-end="366"><strong data-start="292" data-end="328">Sacred texts / epistemic anchors</strong> (Bible, Qurâ€™an, scientific method).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="367" data-end="437">
<p data-start="369" data-end="437"><strong data-start="369" data-end="393">Normative frameworks</strong> (divine command, sharia, secular ethics).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="438" data-end="515">
<p data-start="440" data-end="515"><strong data-start="440" data-end="479">Communal rituals &amp; trust structures</strong> (church, mosque, lab/university).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="517" data-end="742">As long as one system dominates, the <strong data-start="554" data-end="577">intersubjective web</strong> (shared assumptions, predictability of others) holds. But when multiple contradictory systems coexist at scale and none can override the others, you start to get:</p>
<ol data-start="744" data-end="1081">
<li data-start="744" data-end="858">
<p data-start="747" data-end="858"><strong data-start="747" data-end="778">Fragmentation of legitimacy</strong> â€” who has the authority to decide truth? (Pope, Imam, peer-reviewed journal).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="859" data-end="967">
<p data-start="862" data-end="967"><strong data-start="862" data-end="887">Translation breakdown</strong> â€” concepts donâ€™t carry over cleanly (e.g., sin vs. error vs. cognitive bias).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="968" data-end="1081">
<p data-start="971" data-end="1081"><strong data-start="971" data-end="999">Value incommensurability</strong> â€” what is sacred in one system may be meaningless or even offensive in another.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1083" data-end="1515">This is exactly the <em data-start="1103" data-end="1124">small-scale version</em> of what Pachniewski is talking about in his <strong data-start="1169" data-end="1206">intersubjectivity collapse thesis</strong>: when new minds with alien architectures arrive, their â€œreligionsâ€ (value frameworks, interpretive languages, norms) may not even intersect at the level Christianity/Islam/atheism still do. Humans can fight bloody wars over <em data-start="1431" data-end="1449">partial overlaps</em>; with AI-designed minds, the overlaps could shrink toward zero.</p>
<p data-start="1517" data-end="1712">Thatâ€™s why youâ€™re right to see <strong data-start="1548" data-end="1577">civil wars and world wars</strong> as the natural trajectory of IC. Once shared intersubjectivity breaks, violent conflict becomes the fallback coordination mechanism.</p>
<p data-start="1714" data-end="1933" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to help you <strong data-start="1741" data-end="1785">recast Pachniewskiâ€™s â€œscenariosâ€ section</strong> directly in this religious-conflict frame, so itâ€™s easier to illustrate the leap from theological pluralism â†’ intersubjectivity collapse under AGI?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3