l flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="181">Thatâ€™s a sharp critique â€” youâ€™re calling out the <strong data-start="49" data-end="83">business substrate of Big Tech</strong> rather than just their products. At bottom, nearly all the major players are in the same trade:</p>
<ul data-start="183" data-end="432">
<li data-start="183" data-end="325">
<p data-start="185" data-end="325"><strong data-start="185" data-end="216">Selling compute and storage</strong> (AWS, GCP, Azure, Apple iCloud, Metaâ€™s infrastructure â€” whether to developers, advertisers, or end-users).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="326" data-end="432">
<p data-start="328" data-end="432"><strong data-start="328" data-end="348">Buying attention</strong> (via social feeds, recommendation engines, gamified interfaces, or ad placement).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="434" data-end="754">The manipulative part is what you noticed: they <strong data-start="482" data-end="510">amplify extreme outliers</strong>. If a weight-loss app works for 1 in 10,000, or a self-improvement course â€œtransformsâ€ one charismatic user, the platforms will spotlight that case. With enough scale, even statistically meaningless outcomes become <strong data-start="726" data-end="751">narratives of success</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="756" data-end="801">Meanwhile, criticism gets defanged because:</p>
<ul data-start="802" data-end="1180">
<li data-start="802" data-end="952">
<p data-start="804" data-end="952"><strong data-start="804" data-end="842">Discovery pipelines are controlled</strong> â€” algorithms prioritize â€œstickyâ€ or â€œupliftingâ€ stories that keep people scrolling, not systemic critiques.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="953" data-end="1053">
<p data-start="955" data-end="1053"><strong data-start="955" data-end="977">Critics get buried</strong> â€” either throttled by engagement metrics, or overwhelmed by corporate PR.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1054" data-end="1180">
<p data-start="1056" data-end="1180"><strong data-start="1056" data-end="1079">Hope is commodified</strong> â€” showing that â€œmaybe youâ€™ll be the oneâ€ keeps people feeding attention and money into the system.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1182" data-end="1435">In effect, the companies arenâ€™t just middlemen â€” theyâ€™re <strong data-start="1239" data-end="1266">attention-market makers</strong>. They donâ€™t need most strategies to work; they just need a few glittering anecdotes to keep the cycle spinning, while charging rent on the underlying compute/storage.</p>
<p data-start="1437" data-end="1745" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to help you <strong data-start="1467" data-end="1528">frame this in the same â€œarms raceâ€ logic Mark Miller uses</strong> (i.e., that attention- and compute-selling creates feedback loops where destructive strategies outpace corrective ones)? That way your critique links directly to the intersubjectivity-collapse risks youâ€™re exploring.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.5