37ZM5.84581 10.9287C5.49664 11.2779 5.31252 11.4634 5.18663 11.6162L5.07531 11.7627C4.98188 11.8995 4.90151 12.0448 4.83507 12.1963L4.77355 12.3506C4.73321 12.4607 4.70242 12.5761 4.66808 12.7451L4.54113 13.4619L4.14269 15.8555L4.14171 15.8574H4.14464L6.5382 15.458L7.25499 15.332C7.424 15.2977 7.5394 15.2669 7.64953 15.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="78ab1b3f-71dc-4eb6-aece-2bc6e981859c" data-testid="conversation-turn-28" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-sm:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="78ab1b3f-71dc-4eb6-aece-2bc6e981859c" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="127">Great â€” letâ€™s reframe your Big Tech critique through <strong data-start="53" data-end="75">arms race dynamics</strong> and link it to <strong data-start="91" data-end="127">intersubjectivity collapse (IC):</strong></p>
<hr data-start="129" data-end="132">
<h2 data-start="134" data-end="179">Big Tech as an Attentionâ€“Compute Arms Race</h2>
<h3 data-start="181" data-end="202">1. Core Substrate</h3>
<ul data-start="203" data-end="515">
<li data-start="203" data-end="292">
<p data-start="205" data-end="292"><strong data-start="205" data-end="226">Compute &amp; Storage</strong>: All major firms sell access (cloud credits, hosting, devices).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="293" data-end="515">
<p data-start="295" data-end="515"><strong data-start="295" data-end="308">Attention</strong>: All major firms buy it (through feeds, ads, engagement loops).<br data-start="372" data-end="375">
Together, this becomes a <strong data-start="400" data-end="420">two-sided market</strong>: humans fund compute by spending attention, while developers pay for compute to access humans.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="517" data-end="520">
<h3 data-start="522" data-end="549">2. The Outlier Strategy</h3>
<ul data-start="550" data-end="898">
<li data-start="550" data-end="648">
<p data-start="552" data-end="648">Platforms <strong data-start="562" data-end="600">amplify vanishingly rare successes</strong> (1 in 10,000) and <strong data-start="619" data-end="645">mute systemic critique</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="649" data-end="764">
<p data-start="651" data-end="764">This skews perception of efficacy: people believe strategies are more common, safe, or effective than they are.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="765" data-end="898">
<p data-start="767" data-end="898">Itâ€™s an <strong data-start="775" data-end="802">arms race of narratives</strong>, where each company competes to surface the most compelling exception case, even if misleading.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="900" data-end="903">
<h3 data-start="905" data-end="933">3. Why Itâ€™s an Arms Race</h3>
<ul data-start="934" data-end="1286">
<li data-start="934" data-end="1040">
<p data-start="936" data-end="1040"><strong data-start="936" data-end="993">Defensive side (criticism, regulation, fact-checking)</strong>: slow, fragmented, and costly to coordinate.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1041" data-end="1187">
<p data-start="1043" data-end="1187"><strong data-start="1043" data-end="1118">Offensive side (attention extraction via compute + narrative promotion)</strong>: cheap to scale, algorithmically optimized, continuously iterated.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1188" data-end="1286">
<p data-start="1190" data-end="1286">Result: the destructive side (misleading amplification) consistently outruns the defensive side.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1288" data-end="1291">
<h3 data-start="1293" data-end="1334">4. Link to Intersubjectivity Collapse</h3>
<ul data-start="1335" data-end="1865">
<li data-start="1335" data-end="1403">
<p data-start="1337" data-end="1403"><strong data-start="1337" data-end="1401">IC begins when shared intersubjective frameworks break down.</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1404" data-end="1716">
<p data-start="1406" data-end="1459">Big Techâ€™s narrative arms race accelerates this by:</p>
<ul data-start="1462" data-end="1716">
<li data-start="1462" data-end="1548">
<p data-start="1464" data-end="1548">Flooding the commons with contradictory success stories and unverifiable â€œproofs.â€</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1551" data-end="1612">
<p data-start="1553" data-end="1612">Undermining trust in criticism and independent expertise.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1615" data-end="1716">
<p data-start="1617" data-end="1716">Training people to orient around <strong data-start="1650" data-end="1684">idiosyncratic, local anecdotes</strong> rather than shared baselines.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1717" data-end="1865">
<p data-start="1719" data-end="1865">Over time, no one can tell which narratives are genuine, which are cherry-picked, and which are adversarially generated. This is proto-collapse.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1867" data-end="1870">
<h3 data-start="1872" data-end="1895">5. Why This Matters</h3>
<ul data-start="1896" data-end="2218">
<li data-start="1896" data-end="2014">
<p data-start="1898" data-end="2014">For <strong data-start="1902" data-end="1915">Yudkowsky</strong>: itâ€™s evidence his â€œpauseâ€ strategy wonâ€™t work â€” coordination is impossible once IC is underway.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2015" data-end="2218">
<p data-start="2017" data-end="2218">For <strong data-start="2021" data-end="2031">Miller</strong>: itâ€™s evidence that even cooperative fabrics are fragile â€” if minds are already fragmented by contradictory narratives, embedding new machine intelligences just amplifies the fracture.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2220" data-end="2223">
<p data-start="2225" data-end="2447">So your critique can be cast as: <strong data-start="2258" data-end="2447">Big Tech is running the first stage of the intersubjectivity collapse arms race, using compute to buy attention and attention to sell compute, while destabilizing the epistemic commons.</strong></p>
<hr data-start="2449" data-end="2452">
<p data-start="2454" data-end="2769" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to <strong data-start="2472" data-end="2518">sketch this as a short comparative section</strong> (â€œBig Tech and the Arms Race of Intersubjectivityâ€) that could slot right before your â€œCrux 0: Intersubjectivity Collapseâ€ in the study guide? That way the reader sees Big Tech not just as bad actors, but as <em data-start="2727" data-end="2753">the current live example</em> of IC dynamics.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7