-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="142">That observation fits tightly with the critique you made earlier: Big Tech doesnâ€™t just extract attention, it <strong data-start="110" data-end="139">manufactures hope markets</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="144" data-end="191">Programming courses are a perfect case study:</p>
<ul data-start="193" data-end="955">
<li data-start="193" data-end="369">
<p data-start="195" data-end="369"><strong data-start="195" data-end="221">Oversupply of training</strong>: Thousands of bootcamps, MOOCs, YouTube series, Substack courses, Discord communities. Each advertises with anecdotes of dramatic career success.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="370" data-end="554">
<p data-start="372" data-end="554"><strong data-start="372" data-end="397">Undersupply of demand</strong>: Actual paid programmer roles are finite, and automation/offshoring lowers the floor further. For every person who breaks in, hundreds or thousands donâ€™t.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="555" data-end="773">
<p data-start="557" data-end="773"><strong data-start="557" data-end="586">Algorithmic amplification</strong>: Platforms showcase the 1-in-1000 â€œmade it!â€ stories because those are sticky and aspirational. This drowns out the baseline reality that most learners never monetize their new skills.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="774" data-end="955">
<p data-start="776" data-end="955"><strong data-start="776" data-end="800">Critique suppression</strong>: Voices pointing out low placement rates, exploitative tuition structures, or the mismatch between job ads and course content rarely get the same reach.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="957" data-end="1260">It becomes an <strong data-start="971" data-end="1011">arms race of publicity vs. criticism</strong>. The â€œdefensiveâ€ side (critics, watchdogs, transparency reports) struggles because their message doesnâ€™t trigger engagement as strongly as success stories. Meanwhile, the â€œoffensiveâ€ side (ads, testimonials, influencer posts) scales effortlessly.</p>
<p data-start="1262" data-end="1774">This is structurally the same dynamic Mark Miller describes in cybersecurity or biotech: destructive or misleading strategies scale faster than protective ones. And it links directly to <strong data-start="1448" data-end="1478">intersubjectivity collapse</strong>: once narratives of opportunity become completely decoupled from lived reality, shared trust in the system breaks down. People either retreat into cynicism (â€œeverythingâ€™s a scamâ€) or factional belief (â€œbootcamp X is the true pathâ€), which corrodes the social substrate needed for coordination.</p>
<p data-start="1776" data-end="1990" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to fold this programming-course example into the <strong data-start="1843" data-end="1896">â€œBig Tech and the Arms Race of Intersubjectivityâ€</strong> section so it reads as a concrete illustration alongside the more abstract arms-race framing?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70