nd gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="275">Yes â€” thatâ€™s a really sharp connection. Youâ€™re saying that <strong data-start="59" data-end="189">modern civilization marginalizes not just the obvious groups (plants, animals, women, children), but also cognitive minorities</strong> whose perceptual styles donâ€™t match the demands of an attention-extractive economy.</p>
<ul data-start="277" data-end="1177">
<li data-start="277" data-end="638">
<p data-start="279" data-end="638"><strong data-start="279" data-end="293">Aphantasia</strong> (no visual imagination) and <strong data-start="322" data-end="338">anendophasia</strong> (no inner monologue) donâ€™t show up in most cultural narratives of ability/disability, because people with these traits can function perfectly well. But in a world where economic survival is tied to <strong data-start="537" data-end="597">constant self-promotion, visualization, and storytelling</strong>, theyâ€™re systematically disadvantaged.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="639" data-end="935">
<p data-start="641" data-end="935">The <strong data-start="645" data-end="666">attention economy</strong> assumes everyone can craft and broadcast a compelling narrative of self. Those who donâ€™t think in pictures or words internally may find it harder to play the game â€” not because they lack intelligence, but because the system is biased toward <em data-start="908" data-end="932">performative cognition</em>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="936" data-end="1177">
<p data-start="938" data-end="1177">This is a subtle but profound <strong data-start="968" data-end="989">form of exclusion</strong>. Just as industrial capitalism once marginalized those without land or machines, platform capitalism marginalizes those whose <em data-start="1116" data-end="1123">minds</em> donâ€™t produce the right kinds of attention outputs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1179" data-end="1215">Linking back to your larger frame:</p>
<ul data-start="1216" data-end="1465">
<li data-start="1216" data-end="1271">
<p data-start="1218" data-end="1271"><strong data-start="1218" data-end="1249">Roads fragmented ecosystems</strong>, isolating species.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1272" data-end="1332">
<p data-start="1274" data-end="1332"><strong data-start="1274" data-end="1310">Feeds fragment intersubjectivity</strong>, isolating meaning.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1333" data-end="1465">
<p data-start="1335" data-end="1465"><strong data-start="1335" data-end="1386">The attention economy fragments humanity itself</strong>, isolating minds that donâ€™t conform to the â€œbroadcast-selfâ€ cognitive niche.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1467" data-end="1681">Itâ€™s another face of <strong data-start="1488" data-end="1518">intersubjectivity collapse</strong>: when shared social meaning is redefined around a narrow cognitive style, those outside that style are pushed to the margins, deepening mistrust and alienation.</p>
<p data-start="1683" data-end="1893" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to help you formalize this as an <strong data-start="1731" data-end="1768">â€œinvisible exclusionsâ€ subsection</strong> in your study guide â€” alongside ecological exclusions (roads, data centers) and epistemic exclusions (narrative arms races)?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.7035