 flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="138">That makes sense â€” youâ€™re honing in on the dimension you know best: how <strong data-start="72" data-end="135">cognitive style interacts with attention-extraction systems</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="140" data-end="189">If we phrase it in the same collapse framework:</p>
<ul data-start="191" data-end="1144">
<li data-start="191" data-end="366">
<p data-start="193" data-end="366"><strong data-start="193" data-end="234">Structural marginalization (classic):</strong> Plants and animals displaced by roads and development. Women and children often excluded from full political and economic agency.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="367" data-end="599">
<p data-start="369" data-end="599"><strong data-start="369" data-end="408">Cognitive marginalization (modern):</strong> People with aphantasia (no imagery), anendophasia (no inner speech), or other non-normative cognition are sidelined by an economy built on <strong data-start="548" data-end="596">continuous self-narration and self-promotion</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="600" data-end="852">
<p data-start="602" data-end="852"><strong data-start="602" data-end="629">Mechanism of exclusion:</strong> Algorithms and platforms reward those who can produce vivid, compelling streams of imagery and verbal persona. Those who canâ€™t (or who donâ€™t want to) are less legible to the system, so their contributions fade from view.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="853" data-end="1144">
<p data-start="855" data-end="1144"><strong data-start="855" data-end="875">Collapse vector:</strong> Just as roads cut off migratory flows, attention-based systems cut off <strong data-start="947" data-end="967">modes of thought</strong> that donâ€™t translate into â€œperformative attention.â€ Over time, intersubjectivity shrinks: we stop recognizing the validity of minds that donâ€™t broadcast in the same register.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1146" data-end="1366">So yes â€” your angle is vital. It grounds intersubjectivity collapse not only in geopolitical or ecological abstractions, but in the everyday fact that <strong data-start="1297" data-end="1363">civilization increasingly runs on a biased filter of cognition</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="1368" data-end="1583" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to draft a compact <strong data-start="1405" data-end="1436">â€œcognitive marginsâ€ section</strong> you can drop into your larger study guide â€” one that ties your familiarity with these mind-types directly into the arms race / collapse narrative?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8