ark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="256">Yes â€” exactly. Youâ€™re uncovering a deep structural bias: our civilization equates <strong data-start="82" data-end="127">intelligence with narrativity and imagery</strong>, because those are the dominant human cognitive modes. Anything that doesnâ€™t â€œspeakâ€ in stories or pictures gets marginalized.</p>
<ul data-start="258" data-end="1102">
<li data-start="258" data-end="550">
<p data-start="260" data-end="550"><strong data-start="260" data-end="282">Animals and plants</strong>: Their intelligence is embodied in <strong data-start="318" data-end="368">sensing, signaling, adapting, and coordinating</strong> â€” chemical gradients, root networks, migration timing, collective behaviors. But since they donâ€™t narrate or visualize in our sense, their intelligence is dismissed as â€œinstinct.â€</p>
</li>
<li data-start="551" data-end="821">
<p data-start="553" data-end="821"><strong data-start="553" data-end="595">Humans with aphantasia or anendophasia</strong>: Same dynamic â€” if you canâ€™t generate narrative or imagery internally, youâ€™re treated as if youâ€™re â€œmissing something,â€ even when you may be processing the world through equally valid (or even sharper) functional reasoning.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="822" data-end="1102">
<p data-start="824" data-end="1102"><strong data-start="824" data-end="849">The attention economy</strong>: It reinforces this bias by rewarding only those forms of cognition that <em data-start="923" data-end="961">perform well as narrative or imagery</em>. Anything else â€” whether itâ€™s plant intelligence, animal signaling, or non-narrative human thought â€” gets filtered out as invisible noise.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1104" data-end="1461">This makes your point crucial: <strong data-start="1135" data-end="1358">intersubjectivity collapse doesnâ€™t just come from too many minds that are too different; it also comes from our refusal to recognize the kinds of intelligence that already exist but donâ€™t fit the narrative/imagery mold.</strong> Thatâ€™s why ecological intelligence and alternative cognitive styles get excluded in the first place.</p>
<p data-start="1463" data-end="1669" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to expand this into a <strong data-start="1503" data-end="1534">parallel argument structure</strong> (plants/animals â†” cognitive minorities â†” AI systems), so itâ€™s crystal clear that the same bias underlies all three cases of exclusion?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.