dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="216">Yes â€” and thatâ€™s a really fertile extension. If we think in terms of Michael Levinâ€™s â€œmind blindness,â€ then religions can be seen as <strong data-start="133" data-end="213">narrative architectures that encode values, but only in their own modalities</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start="218" data-end="623">
<li data-start="218" data-end="356">
<p data-start="220" data-end="356"><strong data-start="220" data-end="236">Christianity</strong>: frames moral order through <em data-start="265" data-end="314">stories of sacrifice, forgiveness, eternal life</em>. Its intelligence is narrative-ethical.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="357" data-end="468">
<p data-start="359" data-end="468"><strong data-start="359" data-end="368">Islam</strong>: frames order through <em data-start="391" data-end="427">submission, law, rhythmic practice</em>. Its intelligence is juridical-ritual.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="469" data-end="623">
<p data-start="471" data-end="623"><strong data-start="471" data-end="502">Atheism/secular rationalism</strong>: frames order through <em data-start="525" data-end="581">empirical consistency, falsifiability, systematization</em>. Its intelligence is analytic-critical.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="625" data-end="939">Each of these modes produces a <strong data-start="656" data-end="695">different kind of intersubjectivity</strong>. They overlap (all attempt to orient human beings toward meaning, morality, and collective life), but theyâ€™re also <strong data-start="811" data-end="830">incommensurable</strong> in key respects. What looks like â€œtruthâ€ in one narrative can look like â€œnonsenseâ€ or â€œheresyâ€ in another.</p>
<p data-start="941" data-end="1009">Thatâ€™s where the connection to intersubjectivity collapse emerges:</p>
<ul data-start="1010" data-end="1525">
<li data-start="1010" data-end="1225">
<p data-start="1012" data-end="1225">Just as we overlook plant or animal intelligence because it doesnâ€™t communicate in our symbols, <strong data-start="1108" data-end="1222">we overlook the value inherent in rival religious narratives because they donâ€™t â€œspeakâ€ our cognitive language</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1226" data-end="1396">
<p data-start="1228" data-end="1396">A Christian may be mind-blind to the epistemic dignity of an atheistâ€™s stance, just as a secular scientist may be mind-blind to the lived coherence in Islamic ritual.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1397" data-end="1525">
<p data-start="1399" data-end="1525">The collapse risk comes when <strong data-start="1428" data-end="1473">mutual illegibility hardens into mistrust</strong>, and mistrust escalates into factionalism or war.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1527" data-end="1748">In your framework, this means that <strong data-start="1562" data-end="1657">religions are not just competing truth-claims; theyâ€™re competing modalities of intelligence</strong>, each vulnerable to being ignored or suppressed because of our bias toward our own mode.</p>
<p data-start="1750" data-end="1971" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to expand this into a <strong data-start="1790" data-end="1814">three-layer parallel</strong> (plants/animals, cognitive minorities, religious systems), showing how mind blindness operates across all three and ties back to intersubjectivity collapse?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8