k:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="177">Alright â€” hereâ€™s a formal sketch of an <strong data-start="39" data-end="96">Effective Assembly Index for Mind Recognition (EAIMR)</strong> that you can integrate into your RSVP or intersubjectivity collapse framework:</p>
<hr data-start="179" data-end="182">
<h3 data-start="184" data-end="243">Effective Assembly Index for Mind Recognition (EAIMR)</h3>
<p data-start="245" data-end="594"><strong data-start="245" data-end="259">Definition</strong><br data-start="259" data-end="262">
The <em data-start="266" data-end="313">Effective Assembly Index for Mind Recognition</em> is a measure of the improbability of a structure, behavior, or system arising from unguided physical processes, adjusted for the presence of <strong data-start="455" data-end="504">reuse, parallelism, degeneracy, and coherence</strong>. A high EAIMR suggests the presence of a <em data-start="546" data-end="565">mind-like process</em> coordinating the assembly.</p>
<hr data-start="596" data-end="599">
<p data-start="601" data-end="623"><strong data-start="601" data-end="621">Formal Structure</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>EAIMR</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>â€…â€Š</mtext><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>â‹…</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>â‹…</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>â‹…</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{EAIMR}(X) \;=\; \frac{A(X)}{R(X) \cdot P(X) \cdot D(X)} \cdot C(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">EAIMR</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.363em; vertical-align: -0.936em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.427em;"><span style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">â‹…</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">â‹…</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.936em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">â‹…</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="705" data-end="713">Where:</p>
<ul data-start="715" data-end="1540">
<li data-start="715" data-end="839">
<p data-start="717" data-end="839"><strong data-start="717" data-end="729"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></strong> = Raw Assembly Index of structure/system <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span></span></span></span><br data-start="776" data-end="779">
(minimum steps required to build <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span></span></span></span> from primitives).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="841" data-end="1015">
<p data-start="843" data-end="1015"><strong data-start="843" data-end="855"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></strong> = <em data-start="858" data-end="872">Reuse factor</em>: the extent to which pre-assembled modules (motifs, subroutines, ecological niches) are leveraged. Higher reuse lowers effective difficulty.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1017" data-end="1178">
<p data-start="1019" data-end="1178"><strong data-start="1019" data-end="1031"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">P</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></strong> = <em data-start="1034" data-end="1054">Parallelism factor</em>: the degree to which independent assembly steps can occur simultaneously. Higher parallelism lowers effective difficulty.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1180" data-end="1343">
<p data-start="1182" data-end="1343"><strong data-start="1182" data-end="1194"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></strong> = <em data-start="1197" data-end="1216">Degeneracy factor</em>: the number of functionally equivalent alternatives to <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span></span></span></span>. High degeneracy spreads probability mass, lowering difficulty.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1345" data-end="1540">
<p data-start="1347" data-end="1540"><strong data-start="1347" data-end="1359"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(X)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></strong> = <em data-start="1362" data-end="1380">Coherence factor</em>: a multiplier reflecting functional integration, adaptivity, or goal-directedness of the system. Higher coherence boosts recognition of mind-like properties.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1542" data-end="1545">
<p data-start="1547" data-end="1567"><strong data-start="1547" data-end="1565">Interpretation</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1569" data-end="1804">
<li data-start="1569" data-end="1685">
<p data-start="1571" data-end="1685"><strong data-start="1571" data-end="1585">High EAIMR</strong> â†’ unlikely to be explained by blind physics; suggests cognitive, agentic, or mind-like processes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1686" data-end="1804">
<p data-start="1688" data-end="1804"><strong data-start="1688" data-end="1701">Low EAIMR</strong> â†’ plausibly explained by physical self-organization or stochastic assembly without mind-like agency.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1806" data-end="1809">
<p data-start="1811" data-end="1825"><strong data-start="1811" data-end="1823">Examples</strong></p>
